WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:01.870
If you only saw them on their big day

00:00:01.870 --> 00:00:04.390
every February, you might
think that groundhogs

00:00:04.390 --> 00:00:06.260
are pretty shy animals.

00:00:06.260 --> 00:00:08.340
They're actually anything but.

00:00:09.470 --> 00:00:12.360
What started out as a funny sight

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:15.440
turned a little bit scary
for a man from Hampton.

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:17.480
You see those teeth on that guy?

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:20.130
Imagine finding this at your front door.

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:26.040
They might be called ground...hogs,

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:28.820
but they're not related to hogs at all.

00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:33.020
They're actually the largest
species in the squirrel family,

00:00:33.020 --> 00:00:35.290
and they are equally ubiquitous.

00:00:35.290 --> 00:00:39.720
You can find groundhogs all
over the central and eastern US.

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:44.560
In Arkansas, for example,
there's an estimated 67,000.

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:48.600
That's about one groundhog
for every 45 humans.

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:52.360
And wherever they are, they
make their presence known.

00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:53.385
Similar to beavers,

00:00:53.385 --> 00:00:56.550
groundhogs have rapidly growing incisors,

00:00:56.550 --> 00:01:00.030
which they keep from growing
too long by chewing and gnawing

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:02.790
on just about anything they
can get their teeth on,

00:01:02.790 --> 00:01:07.400
including cables, hoses,
and other rubbery materials.

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:09.980
One groundhog reportedly chewed the wires

00:01:09.980 --> 00:01:12.310
inside of a car in Nebraska,

00:01:12.310 --> 00:01:16.200
costing $1,800 in damage repairs.

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:18.650
But they don't just
wreak havoc aboveground.

00:01:18.650 --> 00:01:21.630
Groundhogs are burrowers by nature.

00:01:21.630 --> 00:01:25.560
They live, breed, and
hibernate underground.

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:28.280
But before they can do
that, they have to dig,

00:01:28.280 --> 00:01:33.000
and dig, and dig, and
dig, and dig, and dig.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:36.030
Their tunnels can be anywhere
from half a meter deep

00:01:36.030 --> 00:01:38.140
to 1 1/2 meters deep,

00:01:38.140 --> 00:01:41.270
and they can be up to 18 meters long.

00:01:41.270 --> 00:01:43.730
That's about as long as a bowling lane.

00:01:43.730 --> 00:01:45.580
Their burrows can harm crops,

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:47.330
weaken foundations of buildings,

00:01:47.330 --> 00:01:50.400
and damage farm equipment
that may fall in.

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:54.363
In one case, it's been said
they dug up bones in a cemetery.

00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:58.590
But even if you don't have a lot of land,

00:01:58.590 --> 00:02:01.300
your home could still be a target.

00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:03.440
Groundhogs like grassy open areas

00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:05.260
because they don't have big obstacles

00:02:05.260 --> 00:02:08.460
like tree roots and giant rocks.

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:12.460
So that pretty little garden
or that freshly mowed lawn,

00:02:12.460 --> 00:02:15.840
that is a free-for-all for groundhogs.

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:18.080
And a fence won't keep them out either

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:21.650
'cause they could just burrow
underneath it or climb over.

00:02:21.650 --> 00:02:25.450
Yeah, that's right,
groundhogs can climb too.

00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:27.460
For example, during
floods, they've been known

00:02:27.460 --> 00:02:31.070
to climb chain-link fences
to escape rising water.

00:02:31.070 --> 00:02:32.730
And just about the only
way to keep them out

00:02:32.730 --> 00:02:37.700
is an electric fence, which
can cost between $100 and $350

00:02:37.700 --> 00:02:39.800
depending on the size of your yard.

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:42.790
And removing a groundhog
from your property?

00:02:42.790 --> 00:02:45.210
Getting a wildlife control
professional to help

00:02:45.210 --> 00:02:49.900
could cost about $400 per groundhog!

00:02:49.900 --> 00:02:52.220
Worst comes to worst,
you definitely don't want

00:02:52.220 --> 00:02:54.490
to try and handle them on your own

00:02:54.490 --> 00:02:57.850
since some groundhogs can be
pretty aggressive animals.

00:02:57.850 --> 00:03:01.080
For example, in 2018, a
groundhog chased a woman

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:03.460
in the parking lot of her office building.

00:03:03.460 --> 00:03:05.660
Luckily, she made it to her car.

00:03:05.660 --> 00:03:08.180
But even then, when her
coworkers came to help her,

00:03:08.180 --> 00:03:10.823
the groundhog forced them
to retreat back inside.

00:03:11.730 --> 00:03:15.210
Even worse, groundhogs have
been known to carry rabies,

00:03:15.210 --> 00:03:18.800
which can make them even more
aggressive and dangerous.

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:22.373
So maybe don't keep them near your face.

